# Writing style

## No em dashes

Never use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) in:

- User-facing UI copy
- Legal and marketing text
- Source comments
- Documentation, README, AGENTS.md
- Cursor rules and skills

## How to rewrite

Do not replace an em dash with a hyphen by default. Rewrite the sentence with ordinary punctuation:

- Use a period when the second part is its own clause.
- Use a comma or semicolon for a related aside.
- Use a colon when introducing an explanation or list.
- Use parentheses for a short clarifying remark.

### Examples

```text
Bad:  Helvety can't read or recover them — there's no master key.
Good: Helvety can't read or recover them. There is no master key.

Bad:  Privacy — Helvety cannot decrypt your data.
Good: Privacy: Helvety cannot decrypt your data.
```

## Before finishing text changes

Search active files for `—`. Ignore only immutable applied migrations under `supabase/migrations/`.
